      {
        "name": "18-interview-questions-and-drills",
        "type": "directory",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "README.md",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "# 18 — High-Yield PostgreSQL DBA & Backend Interview Drills\n\n## 🧠 Top 10 Gotchas\n1. **Transaction ID Wraparound**: 32-bit transaction IDs wrap around after 2 billion transactions; requires freeze autovacuum.\n2. **Index Bloat After Massive Deletes**: B-Tree pages are not returned to OS without `REINDEX CONCURRENTLY` or `pg_repack`.\n3. **`COUNT(*)` Performance**: PostgreSQL must inspect visibility of each tuple (MVCC); requires sequential scan unless index-only scan visibility map is clean.\n4. **Connection Memory Leak**: 500 direct connections consume 5GB+ RAM; always use PgBouncer in transaction mode.\n5. **`work_mem` Allocation**: Allocated per sort/hash operation per query node, not per connection.\n6. **GIN Index Update Overhead**: GIN indexes have higher write latency than B-Trees due to pending list inserts.\n7. **`SERIALIZABLE` vs `REPEATABLE READ`**: SSI detects serialization anomalies and aborts with error 40001 (requires client retry loop).\n8. **HOT Updates Prerequisite**: Heap-Only Tuples work only if updated columns are NOT indexed and the block has free space.\n9. **Partition Pruning**: Disabled if WHERE clause contains non-immutable function expressions.\n10. **Lock Queue Head Blocking**: An ungranted `ACCESS EXCLUSIVE` lock request blocks all subsequent reads in queue.\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "example.sql",
            "type": "file",
            "content": "-- 18: Master Interview Drill Summary\nSELECT '1. MVCC xmin/xmax tuple visibility' AS topic\nUNION ALL SELECT '2. Autovacuum transaction ID wraparound'\nUNION ALL SELECT '3. EXPLAIN BUFFERS shared hits vs disk reads'\nUNION ALL SELECT '4. SKIP LOCKED job queue pattern';\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "exercise",
            "type": "directory",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "starter.sql",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "-- TODO: Master Drill: Implement a complete transactional FIFO queue schema with SKIP LOCKED support.\n-- FILL HERE\n"
              },
              {
                "name": "solution.sql",
                "type": "file",
                "content": "CREATE TABLE job_queue (\n    job_id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    payload JSONB NOT NULL,\n    status VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PENDING',\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- Worker query:\n-- BEGIN;\n-- SELECT job_id, payload FROM job_queue \n-- WHERE status = 'PENDING' \n-- ORDER BY job_id ASC \n-- LIMIT 1 \n-- FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED;\n-- UPDATE job_queue SET status = 'PROCESSING' WHERE job_id = <job_id>;\n-- COMMIT;\n"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
